            <div xml:id="d474">

                <pb facs="0423" n="411" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg411"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.852/84: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Daniels</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-04-19T17:00:00-06:00">April 19, 1940—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9:06 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>135. Referring to my despatch No. 10,394 April 11.<anchor n="5" xml:id="d474-f1"
                    /> Sale of SS <hi rendition="#italic">Tine Asmussen</hi> confirmed by W. R.
                    Davis Company as effective yesterday. Terms said by manager Dutch Shell Company
                    as $75,000 one month from date of sale and $150,000 worth of gasoline to be
                    delivered at Houston, Texas. Piatt oil gram price to prevail on date of delivery
                    at Houston. These terms are being checked.</p>
                <p>Finance Minister<anchor n="6" xml:id="d474-f2"/> said purchase has been
                    consummated in accordance with principles international law and facts are being
                    communicated to British and French Governments with view to obtaining their
                    position in the matter.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Daniels</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
